case('EO:8083','Extending the Provisions of the Civil Service Retirement Act to Certain Federal Employees, and Amending Civil Service Rule II','1939-04-10',[1577],
 'PDF p1: EO begins in left column, continues at top of middle column, and ends [No.8083], FR Doc39-1214. The April5,1939 trade-agreements letter beginning below is a different instrument.',[
 item('8083-1',1,'printed p1577, left column','The provisions of the Civil Service Retirement Act of May 29, 1930 (46 Stat. 470), are hereby extended to apply (1) to all Federal employees who have been or may be appointed to any position named in Schedule A or Schedule B of the Civil Service Rules, or to any position excepted by law or Executive order from the operation of the Civil Service Act and Rules, provided that such employees have been or shall be appointed pursuant to the provisions of subdivision (d) of section 3 of Civil Service Rule II, and (2) to all employees who have been or may be accorded a classified status while serving in such positions.','Two eligible classes under one retirement-coverage extension. Both retrospective and prospective phrasing must remain; this is not a single named-person act.'),
 item('8083-2',1,'printed p1577, left column','Subdivision (d) of section 3 of Civil Service Rule II is hereby amended to read as follows:','Replacement amendment; the full following quotation is part of the operative content.','amendment_introducer'),
 item('8083-2a',1,'printed p1577, left column, replacement text','The proper appointing officer may fill any position named in Schedule A or Schedule B, or any other excepted position, as classified positions are filled, in which case the person so appointed shall be eligible for transfer, reinstatement, or promotion to positions in the classified service, subject to the provisions of these rules.','Permission to appoint and resulting eligibility, expressly subject to the rules; retained substantive replacement rule.'),
 item('8083-2b',1,'printed p1577, left column, replacement text','The incumbent of any excepted position so filled will not be entitled to protection against removal afforded by these rules.','Distinct limitation on removal protection within the replacement rule; cannot omit as mere background.'),
 item('8083-3',1,'printed p1577, top middle column','Executive Order No. 3375 of December 24, 1920, extending the provisions of the Civil Service Retirement Act of May 22, 1920, to certain Federal employees, is hereby superseded.','Express supersession separate from retirement extension and replacement of RuleII.'),
 item('8083-4',1,'printed p1577, middle column','This order shall become effective on May 1, 1939.','Express effective date applies to this order as a whole.','effective_date')],
 ['Authority recital cites retirement-act section3, Revised Statutes section1753, Civil Service Act1883. Commission recommendation is explanatory, not another command.','Footnote 1 at Civil Service Rule II: "3 F.R. 1519 DI." It is reference context, not order number or extra rule text.','Printed replacement appears "incumbent"; OCR produces "encumbent". Quotes transcribe the visual source with normalized whitespace and removed line-break hyphens.','No later ending or current predicate established. Cannot treat the act of amending/superseding alone as exhausting the continuing coverage/eligibility content.'])
case('EO:8123','Establishing the Lake Moraine Migratory Waterfowl Refuge — North Dakota','1939-05-10',[1996],
 'PDF p4, right column: begins after EO8122 signature/doc block, ends [No.8123], FR Doc39-1606. EO8124 Lake Oliver begins below. The Florence/Half-Way/Hutchinson/Johnson refuge text in other columns belongs to neighboring orders.',[
 item('8123-1',4,'printed p1996, right column','it is ordered that all lands within or controlled by the United States within the following-described area, comprising 320.00 acres, more or less, in Burleigh County, North Dakota, be, and they are hereby, reserved and set apart, subject to valid rights, for the use of the Department of Agriculture as a refuge and breeding ground for migratory birds and other wildlife:','Reservation/use directive with express valid-rights qualification; geographic description is part of the coverage.'),
 item('8123-1a',4,'printed p1996, right column, Fifth Principal Meridian','T. 143 N., R. 78 W., sec. 13, N½.','Land coverage. Visual source says "all lands within or controlled by the United States"; preserve the unusual "within" wording rather than silently replacing with neighbors\' "owned".','geographic_scope'),
 item('8123-2',4,'printed p1996, right column','It is unlawful for any person to pursue, hunt, trap, capture, wilfully disturb, or kill any bird or wild animal of any kind whatsoever within the limits of the refuge, or to enter thereon, except under such rules and regulations as may be prescribed by the Secretary of Agriculture.','Distinct prohibition on wildlife acts and entry; delegated regulatory exception is part of the provision.'),
 item('8123-3',4,'printed p1996, right column','This reservation shall be known as the Lake Moraine Migratory Waterfowl Refuge.','Separate naming direction, with continuing referential effect; not evidence of the legal fate of the reservation.')],
 ['No own footnotes, schedule, attachment or express termination date. No later event established by the original.','The reservation, conduct prohibition/regulatory exception, and naming provision should all be accounted for; grouping into one inventory unit is possible only with complete substantive coverage.','Source phrasing "within or controlled" is awkward and legal effect of that precise wording is not resolved by this examination.'])
