case('EO:8729','Correcting Executive Orders Nos. 8680, 8682, and 8683 of February 14, 1941, Establishing Certain Naval Defensive Sea Areas and Naval Airspace Reservations','1941-04-02',[1791,1792],
 'PDF p1: starts at bottom middle column after Proclamation2471. Continues at top middle column of PDF p2; ends [No.8729], FR Doc41-2468. EO8730 Civil Service amendment begins immediately below. Footnotes1/2 at foot of p2 middle column attach to target-order citations; footnote3 there concerns later military rule.',[
 item('8729-1',1,'printed pp1791–1792, middle-column cross-page paragraph','The phrase “the territorial waters between the extreme high-water marks in the three-mile marine boundaries” occurring in the first paragraph of Executive Orders Nos. 8680, 8682, and 8683 of February 14, 1941, establishing certain naval defensive sea areas and naval airspace reservations, is hereby corrected to read “the territorial waters between the extreme high-water marks and the three-mile marine boundaries”.','Single correction sentence reaching the first paragraph of each of three named targets; replaces "in" with "and". Targets and exact replacement belong in substantive scope.')],
 ['Quotation spans PDF pp1–2, not p1 alone. No new standalone sea-area reservation, later termination, or independent continuing command is expressly created outside corrected target language here.','Footnote1 to EO8680: "6 F.R. 1014." Footnote2 to EO8682 and EO8683: "6 F.R. 1015." These are citations, not text imported from target orders.','The full target orders are not supplied as relevant pages in these source cards; legal implications of correction for target coverage and later lifecycle require additional material.','No own express effective date beyond signature; do not infer retrospective operation solely from label "corrected".'])
case('EO:8930','Establishing a National Indian Institute in the Department of the Interior','1941-11-01',[5613,5614],
 'PDF p1: starts left column at EO heading; recitals include Convention Article X text. Section1 begins bottom left and continues top middle, followed by sections2–3. Section3 continues at top middle of PDF p2, followed sections4–6 and [No.8930], FR Doc41-8262. EO8931 Panama Canal begins below and continues right; CCC rules are unrelated.',[
 item('8930-recital-X1',1,'printed p5613, left column, Convention Article X quoted paragraph1','The nations subscribing to this Convention shall, on such date as they may deem advisable and within their respective jurisdictions, organize National Indian Institutes. The functions of said Institutes shall, by and large, consist in stimulating interest in and furnishing information about Indian matters to any persons and to public and private institutions. Such National Institutes shall further carry out any studies on these questions that may be of particular interest to the nation concerned.','Quoted convention context includes timing discretion, functions, and study language. Not to be mistaken for numbered sections of the EO or silently discarded from source review.','embedded_convention'),
 item('8930-recital-X2',1,'printed p5613, left column, Convention Article X quoted paragraph2','National Indian Institutes shall be affiliated to the Inter-American Indian Institute, to which they shall submit an annual report.','Treaty/convention recital of affiliation/reporting; EO sections1 and2(g) separately implement these matters.','embedded_convention'),
 item('8930-recital-X3',1,'printed p5613, left column, Convention Article X quoted paragraph3','The financing, organization and regulations of said National Indian Institutes shall be matters falling exclusively within the purview of the respective Governments;','Domestic-government financing/organization/regulations qualification; not an EO appropriation.','embedded_convention'),
 item('8930-1',1,'printed p5613, section1 left-to-middle column','There is hereby established in the Department of the Interior a National Indian Institute for the United States of America, which Institute shall be affiliated with the Inter-American Indian Institute.','Establish institution and direct affiliation; two operative components, not merely a one-time establishment caption.'),
 item('8930-2a',1,'printed p5613, middle column, section2(a)','Initiate and promote collaboration in the fields of Indian administration and the study of the Indian among Federal, State and private agencies, learned societies, and scholars in the United States, and the Inter-American Indian Institute, and through the Institute with governmental agencies, learned societies and scholars in the other American countries.','Institute shall perform this collaboration function.'),
 item('8930-2b',1,'printed p5613, middle column, section2(b)','Collaborate with the Inter-American Indian Institute, learned societies, and foundations in the coordination, development, and administration of research projects and studies relating to the Indian.','Separate required research-collaboration function.'),
 item('8930-2c',1,'printed p5613, middle column, section2(c)','Maintain liaison between agencies of the United States Government directly or indirectly concerned with Indian administration or Indian studies in this or other countries for the purpose of coordinating cooperation by the United States with other American nations in regard to Indian matters.','Separate liaison/coordination function.'),
 item('8930-2d',1,'printed p5613, middle column, section2(d)','Direct the preparation and publication of materials dealing with Indian administration in the United States of interest to the other American nations, and to publish such other materials as may be required in connection with authorized activities.','Publication preparation/direction and publishing function, with authorized-activities qualifier.'),
 item('8930-2e',1,'printed p5613, middle column, section2(e)','Assemble and prepare library material and bibliographies dealing with Indian problems.','Library/bibliography function.'),
 item('8930-2f',1,'printed p5613, middle column, section2(f)','Collaborate with the Inter-American Indian Institute in planning for the Inter-American Conference on Indian Life.','Conference-planning collaboration; source does not establish the conference occurred or all planning ceased.'),
 item('8930-2g',1,'printed p5613, middle column, section2(g)','Submit an annual report to the Inter-American Indian Institute.','Recurring annual report, not a date that terminates the institution or all functions.'),
 item('8930-3a',1,'printed p5613, middle column, section3','The Institute shall be managed by a Director who, with other necessary employees, shall be appointed by the Secretary of the Interior, and its functions shall be administered in the Bureau of Indian Affairs.','Management, appointment authority/duty, and BIA administration are distinct components.'),
 item('8930-3b',1,'printed pp5613–5614, middle-column cross-page continuation of section3','The Institute shall use insofar as practicable such informational, fiscal, personnel, and other general business services and facilities as may be made available through the Interior Department or other agencies of the Government.','Service/facility-use duty qualified by practicability and availability. Continuation on p2 must remain.'),
 item('8930-4',2,'printed p5614, middle column, section4','There is hereby established a Policy Board of the Institute which shall recommend policies to be followed by the Institute, and which shall be composed of:','Establishment plus continuing recommendation and composition provisions; the following six items are part of scope.'),
 item('8930-4a',2,'printed p5614, section4(a)','The Commissioner of Indian Affairs.','Ex officio composition requirement.','composition'),
 item('8930-4b',2,'printed p5614, section4(b)','Two or more members, who may be public officers or private citizens, to be appointed by the Secretary of the Interior, at least one of whom shall be an Indian.','Minimum number, appointment authority and at-least-one-Indian condition.','composition'),
 item('8930-4c',2,'printed p5614, section4(c)','One representative designated by the Secretary of State.','Required representative/designator.','composition'),
 item('8930-4d',2,'printed p5614, section4(d)','One representative designated by the Secretary of Agriculture.','Required representative/designator.','composition'),
 item('8930-4e',2,'printed p5614, section4(e)','One representative designated by the Smithsonian Institution.','Required representative/designator.','composition'),
 item('8930-4f',2,'printed p5614, section4(f)','One representative designated by the Librarian of Congress.','Required representative/designator.','composition'),
 item('8930-4optional',2,'printed p5614, section4, following paragraph/list','In addition to the foregoing, one representative may be designated as a member of the Board by each of the following organizations: The National Research Council. The Social Science Research Council. The American Council of Learned Societies.','Optional representation by each named organization; permission differs from mandatory core composition.'),
 item('8930-5',2,'printed p5614, middle column, section5','The Chairman of the Board, who shall be designated by the Secretary of the Interior, shall call meetings of the Board, and, subject to the approval of the Board, may establish advisory committees and may designate, as affiliates of the Institute, learned societies and other organizations concerned with the study of the Indian and with Indian welfare.','Chair designation, duty to call meetings, and Board-approval-qualified permissions for committees/affiliates all retained.'),
 item('8930-6',2,'printed p5614, middle column, section6','The members of the Board and the advisory committees may be reimbursed for necessary traveling expenses and subsistence, as provided by law.','Reimbursement permission limited by necessity, categories, and law; independent substantive provision.')],
 ['Recitals state Senate advice/consentMay26,1941, convention openedMexicoCityNovember1,1940, USsignedNovember29,1940, PresidentratifiedJune6,1941. These historical recitals are not later execution evidence for EO duties.','Another recital states DOI charged by law with supervision/management of all Indian affairs. It provides authority/context and is not itself a new order to assume every Indian-affairs function.','No separate attachment or full convention is appended on the two relevant pages; only ArticleX is quoted. This examination does not decide treaty independent legal force or all convention obligations without full treaty context.','No own footnotes or express sunset. Creation, affiliation, seven section2 functions, management/appointments/BIA administration, service use, policy board/composition, chair/meetings/committees/affiliates, and reimbursement all need substantive accounting.','No conclusion that any command was discharged or terminated follows merely from establishment, historical annual reports, reorganization or passage of time; later evidence not examined.'])
case('EO:13613','Providing an Order of Succession Within the Department of Commerce','2012-05-21',[31155,31156],
 'Two-page order-specific PDF. PDF p1 contains authority recital and sections1–3; PDF p2 contains section4, signature/date, FR Doc2012-12882. No neighboring instrument text or annex within supplied PDF.',[
 item('13613-1',1,'printed p31155, section1','Subject to the provisions of section 2 of this order, and to the limitations set forth in the Act, the following officials of the Department of Commerce, in the order listed, shall act as and perform the functions and duties of the office of the Secretary of Commerce (Secretary) during any period in which the Secretary has died, resigned, or otherwise become unable to perform the functions and duties of the office of the Secretary:','Conditional ordered succession duty, expressly subject to exceptions and FVRA; all nine ranked offices are material.'),
 item('13613-1list',1,'printed p31155, section1(a)–(i)','(a) Deputy Secretary of Commerce; (b) General Counsel of the Department of Commerce; (c) Under Secretary of Commerce for International Trade; (d) Under Secretary of Commerce for Economic Affairs; (e) Under Secretary of Commerce for Standards and Technology; (f) Under Secretary of Commerce for Oceans and Atmosphere and Administrator of the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration; (g) Under Secretary of Commerce for Export Administration; (h) Chief Financial Officer of the Department of Commerce and Assistant Secretary of Commerce (Administration); and (i) The Boulder Laboratories Site Manager, National Institute of Standards and Technology.','Ranked offices; nine subitems are a hierarchy within the succession provision, not nine separate unrelated directives.','ranked_scope'),
 item('13613-2a',1,'printed p31155, section2(a)','No individual who is serving in an office listed in section 1(a)–(i) of this order in an acting capacity shall, by virtue of so serving, act as Secretary pursuant to this order.','Exclusion of acting occupants by virtue of acting status.'),
 item('13613-2b',1,'printed p31155, section2(b)','No individual listed in section 1(a)–(i) of this order shall act as Secretary unless that individual is otherwise eligible to so serve under the Act, as amended.','Statutory eligibility condition distinct from acting-occupant exclusion.'),
 item('13613-2c',1,'printed p31155, section2(c)','Notwithstanding the provisions of this order, the President retains discretion, to the extent permitted by law, to depart from this order in designating an acting Secretary.','Express retained presidential discretion within legal limits.'),
 item('13613-3',1,'printed p31155, section3','Executive Order 13242 of December 18, 2001 (Providing An Order of Succession Within the Department of Commerce) and Memorandum for the Secretary of Commerce of October 3, 2002 (Designation of Officers of the Department of Commerce to Act as Secretary of Commerce) are hereby revoked.','Express revocation of both a numbered EO and unnumbered dated memorandum.'),
 item('13613-4',2,'printed p31156, section4','This order is not intended to, and does not, create any right or benefit, substantive or procedural, enforceable at law or in equity by any party against the United States, its departments, agencies, or entities, its officers, employees, or agents, or any other person.','Judicial-review/noncreation limitation is substantive source context; retained separately even if not an affirmative duty.')],
 ['Authority recital includes FVRA1998 as amended5USC3345etseq. It incorporates statutory limitations; the underlying statute is not independently examined in this source-card-only phase.','No separate general-provisions section, implementation/funding command, effective-date paragraph, or attachment appears. Section4 is on second page and must not disappear from complete inventory.','No later revocation/current predicate search was performed. Source-only reading cannot establish status at2026-10-14.'])
